This product is a Cangjie (仓颉) / HarmonyOS port of the EU Digital Identity
Wallet kit (protocol facade / integration hub) for Swift:

    eudi-lib-ios-wallet-kit
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-ios-wallet-kit

The EudiWallet facade and its issuance / presentation / storage / support
service layers are reimplemented in Cangjie with the original Swift sources
used as the reference implementation.

This product depends on and/or bundles the following third-party software
(all consumed as pinned third_party clones; Apache-2.0 unless noted):

  - eudi_lib_mdoc_data_model    — Document / DeviceResponse / DeviceRequest types
  - eudi_lib_mdoc_security      — SecureArea / session signing
  - eudi_lib_mdoc_transfer      — BLE proximity presentation (mdoc GATT)
  - eudi_lib_wallet_storage     — document + key storage
  - eudi_lib_sdjwt              — SD-JWT credentials
  - eudi_lib_openid4vp_vci      — OpenID4VCI issuance + OpenID4VP presentation engine
  - eudi_lib_statium            — credential status (status list)
  - eudi_lib_jose               — JOSE / JWE
  - eudi_lib_x509               — certificate chain validation
  - eudi_lib_core_crypto        — cryptographic primitives
  - eudi_lib_cbor               — CBOR encoding
  - cangjie-stdx 1.1.3.1 (Apache-2.0) — bundled under entry/libs/stdx/
  - OpenSSL runtime libraries (libcrypto_openssl.z.so, libssl_openssl.z.so)
    and libsecurec.so, bundled under entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ for on-device
    stdx.crypto / HUKS execution (consumed transitively).

